  {
   "id": 648550,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"3\" type=\"1\">\n  <li>Which ball loses its height more quickly, this ball, modeled by <span data-math=\"h(n)=120 \\cdot (\\frac{4}{5})^n\">h(n)=120 \\cdot (\\frac{4}{5})^n</span>, or a tennis ball whose height in inches after <span data-math=\"n\">n</span> bounces is modeled by the function <span data-math=\"f\">f</span>\n where <span data-math=\"f(n)=50 \\cdot (\\frac{5}{9})^n\">f(n)=50 \\cdot (\\frac{5}{9})^n</span>\n?</li>\n</ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1279017,
     "content_html": "the ball modeled by <span data-math=\"h(n)\"></span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1279018,
     "content_html": "the ball modeled by <span data-math=\"f(n)\"></span>"
    }
